    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'll try being lighter with the pressure on the relief cuts. one more thing though—i've noticed that sometimes the grain behaves really unpredictably, almost like it's fighting me, where it'll stay clean for a few cuts and then suddenly blowout in a way that doesn't seem to match the grain direction i see. is there anything else that could be causing that kind of inconsistent behavior in the wood?",
